  "text": "Those are the cleaning steps, and they're much the same in every project. Analysis comes after: counting, tagging, building features. It depends on your goal, and so should the cleaning, because most of its steps are optional. The order you run them in matters, too.\n\nHere's the lesson's tiny test: the word the, written three ways, followed by end is near. Lowercase first, then remove stopwords, and every the is gone. End, near. Remove stopwords first, and all three slip through. The stopword list is all lowercase, and none of the three is. Nothing crashed. You just got a list that looks fine, and is wrong. Order bugs are silent. Every one of these steps works on tokens. So the first step of the pipeline is deciding where one word ends.",
